{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01621",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 1.12,
      "end_seconds": 7.2,
      "duration_seconds": 6.08,
      "text": "All set here, doctor. Chart's updated, and I'll read the readings out when you're ready."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 9.07,
      "end_seconds": 13.13,
      "duration_seconds": 4.06,
      "text": "Perfect, thanks. Hello there, so what's the trouble?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 14.04,
      "end_seconds": 19.52,
      "duration_seconds": 5.48,
      "text": "Doctor, I'll sit in if that's okay, I know what's been happening."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 20.22,
      "end_seconds": 23.89,
      "duration_seconds": 3.67,
      "text": "That's fine, sit down. We'll go through it together."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 25.76,
      "end_seconds": 28.8,
      "duration_seconds": 3.04,
      "text": "We came because of a fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 30.87,
      "end_seconds": 34.38,
      "duration_seconds": 3.51,
      "text": "Can you tell me when it first started?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 36.0,
      "end_seconds": 47.59,
      "duration_seconds": 11.59,
      "text": "Okay, so I'm not sure when it began, to be honest. Some weeks ago, but I can't say how many."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 49.55,
      "end_seconds": 52.17,
      "duration_seconds": 2.62,
      "text": "How much does it limit you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 55.02,
      "end_seconds": 58.41,
      "duration_seconds": 3.39,
      "text": "Right, about a five out of ten."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 60.41,
      "end_seconds": 63.21,
      "duration_seconds": 2.8,
      "text": "How often do you get it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 64.55,
      "end_seconds": 70.98,
      "duration_seconds": 6.43,
      "text": "It's, um... not exactly... well, hard to explain, I mean—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 71.71,
      "end_seconds": 78.65,
      "duration_seconds": 6.94,
      "text": "Let me put it another way: how many times in a typical day or week?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 80.18,
      "end_seconds": 82.76,
      "duration_seconds": 2.58,
      "text": "It happens every other day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 83.76,
      "end_seconds": 90.24,
      "duration_seconds": 6.48,
      "text": "And the other thing I wanted to mention is that I can't really—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 90.34,
      "end_seconds": 95.54,
      "duration_seconds": 5.2,
      "text": "Tell the doctor about the other thing, that's what worries me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 97.5,
      "end_seconds": 105.39,
      "duration_seconds": 7.89,
      "text": "I was getting to that! Mm, I've also had missing school, for two months."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 105.9,
      "end_seconds": 109.36,
      "duration_seconds": 3.46,
      "text": "Okay, how troublesome is it day to day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 111.26,
      "end_seconds": 116.12,
      "duration_seconds": 4.86,
      "text": "Maybe a four out of ten on a bad day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 116.39,
      "end_seconds": 121.62,
      "duration_seconds": 5.23,
      "text": "Sure. Have you had a fever before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 126.48,
      "end_seconds": 134.06,
      "duration_seconds": 7.58,
      "text": "Yes, something like this happened about six months ago, and it went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_5",
      "role": "UNKNOWN",
      "start_seconds": 135.28,
      "end_seconds": 138.74,
      "duration_seconds": 3.46,
      "text": "Yes, that's right, that's how it was."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 140.11,
      "end_seconds": 140.92,
      "duration_seconds": 0.81,
      "text": "Any smoking?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 142.42,
      "end_seconds": 146.26,
      "duration_seconds": 3.84,
      "text": "No, I've never smoked in my life."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 149.96,
      "end_seconds": 151.66,
      "duration_seconds": 1.7,
      "text": "How are your meals?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 153.64,
      "end_seconds": 157.66,
      "duration_seconds": 4.02,
      "text": "I grab fast food at lunch most days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 158.16,
      "end_seconds": 160.61,
      "duration_seconds": 2.45,
      "text": "What's on your current medicine list?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 161.95,
      "end_seconds": 169.56,
      "duration_seconds": 7.61,
      "text": "It's, It's a... um, I can't remember what it's called. It's a small white one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 170.66,
      "end_seconds": 173.38,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "Do you remember what it's for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 175.17,
      "end_seconds": 192.98,
      "duration_seconds": 17.81,
      "text": "For my thyroid, I believe. My husband sets them out for me, I just take what I'm given. Losartan. I take it 50 milligrams, once a day for my blood pressure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 194.3,
      "end_seconds": 195.87,
      "duration_seconds": 1.57,
      "text": "And for how long?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 197.57,
      "end_seconds": 208.05,
      "duration_seconds": 10.48,
      "text": "About about a month. Pantoprazole, 40 milligrams, before breakfast for my acidity. Glycomet. I take it 500 milligrams, maybe, twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 209.94,
      "end_seconds": 213.93,
      "duration_seconds": 3.99,
      "text": "Did you happen to bring the box or the paperwork?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 214.67,
      "end_seconds": 218.9,
      "duration_seconds": 4.23,
      "text": "Not with me. I'll bring it next time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 220.51,
      "end_seconds": 224.42,
      "duration_seconds": 3.91,
      "text": "Any inherited conditions that you know of in the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 229.68,
      "end_seconds": 231.93,
      "duration_seconds": 2.25,
      "text": "My cousin has psoriasis."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 233.87,
      "end_seconds": 236.23,
      "duration_seconds": 2.36,
      "text": "Do you have any chronic illnesses?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 242.31,
      "end_seconds": 245.15,
      "duration_seconds": 2.84,
      "text": "I have an underactive thyroid."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 246.39,
      "end_seconds": 247.09,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Understood."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 248.09,
      "end_seconds": 257.74,
      "duration_seconds": 9.65,
      "text": "High blood pressure, for about a year. I have acid reflux, for about a year. Diabetes, for two years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 263.43,
      "end_seconds": 271.01,
      "duration_seconds": 7.58,
      "text": "Right, so high blood pressure and diabetes are already on your record. We'll keep that in mind today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 279.4,
      "end_seconds": 283.6,
      "duration_seconds": 4.2,
      "text": "Alright, are there any allergies I should be aware of?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 288.59,
      "end_seconds": 290.06,
      "duration_seconds": 1.47,
      "text": "No known allergies."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 292.13,
      "end_seconds": 298.8,
      "duration_seconds": 6.67,
      "text": "Well, I'm not sure that's right. I seem to recall a problem with diclofenac."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 302.59,
      "end_seconds": 305.39,
      "duration_seconds": 2.8,
      "text": "I mean, I don't remember that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 305.97,
      "end_seconds": 315.21,
      "duration_seconds": 9.24,
      "text": "Fair enough, I'll write down both versions. A few quick ones: ear pain, rash, drooling or difficulty breathing?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 316.39,
      "end_seconds": 329.02,
      "duration_seconds": 12.63,
      "text": "No, no ear pain, no rash, no drooling. I did have a sore throat again at one point, but that went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 329.92,
      "end_seconds": 333.9,
      "duration_seconds": 3.98,
      "text": "Okay, has your heart given you any trouble?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 334.99,
      "end_seconds": 336.96,
      "duration_seconds": 1.97,
      "text": "No, that's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 338.28,
      "end_seconds": 339.73,
      "duration_seconds": 1.45,
      "text": "Neurologically, anything strange?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 341.69,
      "end_seconds": 343.92,
      "duration_seconds": 2.23,
      "text": "No, nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 345.33,
      "end_seconds": 353.96,
      "duration_seconds": 8.63,
      "text": "Here are the numbers, doctor. Temperature 38.9, BP is 126 over 67, pulse 101. SpO2 95 percent on room air."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 354.84,
      "end_seconds": 356.23,
      "duration_seconds": 1.39,
      "text": "Good, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 358.08,
      "end_seconds": 361.72,
      "duration_seconds": 3.64,
      "text": "Right, let's have a proper look at you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 362.38,
      "end_seconds": 363.08,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 363.93,
      "end_seconds": 366.7,
      "duration_seconds": 2.77,
      "text": "Take a deep breath for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 379.96,
      "end_seconds": 387.23,
      "duration_seconds": 7.27,
      "text": "The tonsils are large and red with white spots, and the neck glands are tender."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 387.87,
      "end_seconds": 389.38,
      "duration_seconds": 1.51,
      "text": "Yes, that's fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 393.78,
      "end_seconds": 396.0,
      "duration_seconds": 2.22,
      "text": "You can sit up now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 404.93,
      "end_seconds": 412.88,
      "duration_seconds": 7.95,
      "text": "Taking everything into account, my working impression is tonsillitis. I'd also keep a viral sore throat in mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 413.4,
      "end_seconds": 416.24,
      "duration_seconds": 2.84,
      "text": "What are the odds it's serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0061",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 419.76,
      "end_seconds": 452.55,
      "duration_seconds": 32.79,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like tonsillitis, but I'd like to confirm. Let's book a throat swab to look into recurrent tonsillitis. It's a routine test and it'll give us a much clearer picture. What I'm giving you is phenoxymethylpenicillin, 250 milligrams, four times a day, ten days. That's for tonsillitis. Plenty of fluids and soft foods, and he can return to school when the fever has gone."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0062",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 453.29,
      "end_seconds": 474.47,
      "duration_seconds": 21.18,
      "text": "Don't skip meals, and try to eat smaller portions more often through the day. I'm going to send a referral to the ENT clinic. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0063",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 476.95,
      "end_seconds": 480.17,
      "duration_seconds": 3.22,
      "text": "Yes, I'll bear that in mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0064",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 481.0,
      "end_seconds": 487.53,
      "duration_seconds": 6.53,
      "text": "If the symptoms get worse, or you feel really unwell, please come to the emergency department."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0065",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 489.43,
      "end_seconds": 493.7,
      "duration_seconds": 4.27,
      "text": "Um, I know what to watch for."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0066",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 494.27,
      "end_seconds": 500.42,
      "duration_seconds": 6.15,
      "text": "See me again if recurrent, tonsil review. Does all of that make sense?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0067",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 501.25,
      "end_seconds": 504.55,
      "duration_seconds": 3.3,
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense. Thanks for explaining."
    }
  ]
}